        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy for the drive system first. Rear-wheel drive handles most sloped lawns, all-wheel drive is worth the premium when your grades are steep or often damp, and front-wheel drive does not belong on a hill at all. The Toro 22-inch Recycler AWD is our first choice, the EGO LM2156SP is the pick if you want battery power, and the Craftsman M310 is the right kind of cheap for moderate slopes.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then measure your slope, and mow it the right way: across with a walk-behind, up and down with a rider, and never when the grass is wet. No feature on a mower matters as much as those three habits.
          </p>
